#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build the comparison report from native captures, without repainting screenshots."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,re,shutil
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];out=root/'docs/reports/cliff-alternatives'
shutil.copyfile(root/'docs/reports/canyon-formations/target.png',out/'target.png')
labels={'original':'Original — current working version','a':'A — irregular surface triangulation','b':'B — chunky sandstone masses','c':'C — hybrid masses + local fractures'}
stats={}
for mode in labels:
    log=(out/(mode+'.log')).read_text();m=re.search(r'PROTOTYPE triangles=(\d+) masses=(\d+).*?max_vertex_depth_m=([\d.]+) build_ms=([\d.]+)',log)
    if m:stats[mode]={'triangles':int(m[1]),'masses':int(m[2]),'max_depth_m':float(m[3])}
    else:stats[mode]={'triangles':int(re.search(r'original_triangles=(\d+)',log)[1]),'masses':0,'max_depth_m':None}
bench=(out/'original.log').read_text()
for mode,reps,median,minimum,maximum in re.findall(r'BENCH mode=(\w+) repetitions=(\d+) median_ms=([\d.]+) min_ms=([\d.]+) max_ms=([\d.]+)',bench):stats[mode]['build_median_ms']=float(median)
scores={'original':[1,1,1,2,5],'a':[3,4,2,3,4],'b':[2,3,3,2,3],'c':[2,3,3,3,3.5]};weights=[35,20,20,15,10]
for mode in labels:stats[mode]['subjective_scores_0_to_5']=scores[mode];stats[mode]['weighted_score']=sum(v*w/5 for v,w in zip(scores[mode],weights))
(out/'evaluation.json').write_text(json.dumps({'status':'visual_goal_not_yet_met','recommendation':'A is the strongest prototype; no rollout recommended yet','scope':'upper wall between trail posts only','seed':1866,'stats':stats},indent=2)+'\n')
def grid(kind,wire=False):
    cells=[]
    for mode,label in labels.items():
        src=mode+('-wire' if wire else '')+'.png'
        picture=f'<img src="{src}" alt="{label}">' if kind=='full' else f'<div class="crop"><img src="{src}" alt="{label}"></div>'
        cells.append(f'<figure><figcaption>{label}</figcaption><a href="{src}">{picture}</a></figure>')
    return ''.join(cells)
quality=''.join('<tr><th>'+labels[m]+'</th>'+''.join(f'<td>{v:g}</td>' for v in scores[m])+f'<td><strong>{stats[m]["weighted_score"]:g}</strong></td></tr>' for m in labels)
complexity=''.join(f'<tr><th>{labels[m]}</th><td>{s["triangles"]}</td><td>{s["masses"] or "—"}</td><td>{str(round(s["max_depth_m"],3))+" m" if s["max_depth_m"] is not None else "—"}</td><td>{str(round(s["build_median_ms"],3))+" ms" if "build_median_ms" in s else "existing mesh"}</td></tr>' for m,s in stats.items())
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Cliff geometry — three alternatives</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#1c2225;color:#e8e2d7;font:17px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1500px;margin:auto;padding:30px}h1{line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:40px}a{color:#9bdbcf}p{max-width:1120px}code,pre{color:#e6c189}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px}td,th{border-bottom:1px solid #455055;text-align:left;padding:12px}th{font-weight:600}.status{border-left:5px solid #d3a254;background:#293237;padding:18px}.wide{overflow:auto;margin:20px 0}.sheet{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:0;background:#1c2225;width:max-content}.sheet figure{margin:0;border:2px solid #455055}.sheet figcaption{height:40px;padding:5px 16px;font:600 20px/30px system-ui;background:#273238;color:#f1e7d8}.full img{display:block;width:1440px;height:900px}.crop{position:relative;overflow:hidden;width:1220px;height:400px;background:#121719}.crop img{position:absolute;width:2880px;height:1800px;max-width:none;left:-820px;top:-160px;image-rendering:auto}.reference{max-width:1100px;width:100%}.downloads{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap}.note{color:#bdc9c9}.small{font-size:14px}.case{border-top:1px solid #455055;padding-top:12px}
</style><main><h1>Cliff geometry: three isolated alternatives</h1><p class="status"><strong>Checkpoint 4 — stop for review.</strong> A is the strongest of these prototypes. None reproduces the reference well enough to recommend production rollout. This experiment did not replace the production generator or adopt an option.</p><p>Seed 1866 · Works floor · room 2 · original style · native 1440 × 900 · fixed 160% game zoom · 60 simulation frames. Only the front wall above the player, between the two trail posts, is replaced in a separate debug executable. All captures use the normal game's renderer, sun, materials, postprocessing, simulation and camera. No generated or repainted concept images.</p><div class="downloads"><a href="comparison.png">Download four full screenshots (2888 × 1888)</a><a href="wall-comparison.png">Download enlarged wall comparison (2448 × 888)</a><a href="wireframes.png">Download wireframe comparison</a><a href="capture.json">Capture manifest</a><a href="evaluation.json">Evaluation data</a></div><h2>Comparable wall details</h2><p>Exactly the same pixel crop in each native screenshot, enlarged 2× for inspection. This is display magnification, not a different camera zoom. Original top left; A top right; B bottom left; C bottom right.</p><div class="wide"><div id="wall-sheet" class="sheet">'''+grid('crop')+'''</div></div><h2>Full scene</h2><p>The rest of the scene is retained. Changes in cast shadows follow from the new wall geometry. The FPS HUD is a capture-time counter; it is not a controlled performance benchmark.</p><div class="wide"><div id="full-sheet" class="sheet full">'''+grid('full')+'''</div></div><h2>Wireframes</h2><p>The overlays show the same selected wall, using the same renderer and camera as the solid views. The unchanged surrounding cliffs deliberately have no overlay.</p><div class="wide"><div id="wire-sheet" class="sheet">'''+grid('crop',True)+'''</div></div><h2>Visual specification</h2><a href="target.png"><img class="reference" src="target.png" alt="Supplied canyon art-direction reference"></a><p>The supplied target is used for face proportions and natural sandstone forms. It is a different layout, so overall compositions cannot be matched in this fixed-wall experiment.</p><h2>1. Architecture: why the strips survive</h2><p><code>buildCanyonAppearance()</code> in <code>src/world/CanyonAppearance.cpp</code> clips individual source terrain triangles into contour polygons. Its <code>wall()</code> lambda extrudes each contour segment as two triangles. <code>cap()</code> builds the ledges and bevels. This repeats the source grid's short contour edges as full-height seams. The later <code>cliffDetail::build()</code> pass in <code>CliffWallTopology.cpp</code> remeshes only some connected groups; rejected or disconnected sections retain the original pattern. Vertex noise alone does not remove that segmentation.</p><p>The diagnostic selects a connected 39-segment contour between the trail posts: 24.513 m along the wall, average height 2.139 m. It parameterizes this as distance along the wall × normalized vertical height, preserving the original upper and lower contours and fixed end boundaries.</p><h2>2. Prototypes</h2><div class="case"><h3>A — irregular triangulation</h3><p>Boundary-constrained Delaunay triangulation with minimum-distance interior sampling, varying heights, coherent normal displacement and interior contour smoothing. Original upper/lower vertices remain fixed. Flat normals provide the shading.</p><p><strong>Strength:</strong> the clearest removal of the repeated vertical strip pattern with almost unchanged triangle count. <strong>Weakness:</strong> the surface still reads as a triangular mosaic or broken rubble in places; it lacks the reference's primary, broad sandstone masses.</p></div><div class="case"><h3>B — chunky formations</h3><p>Thirteen irregular Voronoi geological sections with inset polyhedral fronts, tilted primary planes and shared seam vertices. Sections interlock as one welded exterior skin; this is not a pile of complete hidden rock solids. Section widths, vertical centers, recesses and depths vary. Displacement is capped and fades to the original boundary.</p><p><strong>Strength:</strong> visibly stronger primary shapes and depth. <strong>Weakness:</strong> bevels and seams produce pointed shards and plate-like forms rather than convincing sandstone. The first uncapped prototype protruded too far; the final capture uses a shallow envelope. This does not solve its art-direction problem.</p></div><div class="case"><h3>C — hybrid</h3><p>Nine larger geological sections with broad primary planes and selectively split fracture faces. Fracture density varies; most primary faces stay coarse. It shares B's boundary-preserving mass skin, with a smaller depth limit.</p><p><strong>Strength:</strong> fewer primary masses, selective detail and fewer triangles than B. <strong>Weakness:</strong> it retains the plate/shard character and some block-like repetition. Added complexity does not make it closer to the supplied target than A.</p></div><h2>3. Weighted visual evaluation</h2><p>Subjective inspection scores, 0–5. These are judgments from the rendered comparisons, not an automated similarity measurement or acceptance test. Geometry complexity is only 10% of the decision.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Target<br>35%</th><th>No strips<br>20%</th><th>Large forms<br>20%</th><th>Low-poly quality<br>15%</th><th>Cost<br>10%</th><th>Weighted /100</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+quality+'''</tbody></table><h2>4. Complexity and validation</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Target-wall triangles</th><th>Masses</th><th>Max vertex movement</th><th>Median build, 21 samples</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+complexity+'''</tbody></table><p>Timings measure only CPU construction of this one prototype, not loading the game, building a floor or rendering it. No GPU draw-call reduction or global performance gain is claimed. The production material grouping is unchanged.</p><p>Each prototype validates chart coverage, edge manifoldness, no open interior edges and fixed outer contour vertices, then rebuilds from the same seed and compares every generated vertex. Unselected triangles are copied unchanged; caps, ground, terrace geometry, decorations and the authoritative collision field are not rewritten. This is visual-only debug substitution. These checks do not establish an art-direction match or a complete world-scale rollout.</p><p>Native builds and all eight captures succeeded. Logs: <a href="build.log">build</a>, <a href="original.log">original + CPU benchmarks</a>, <a href="a.log">A</a>, <a href="b.log">B</a>, <a href="c.log">C</a>, <a href="a-wire.log">A wire</a>, <a href="b-wire.log">B wire</a>, <a href="c-wire.log">C wire</a>. No WASM check: native rendering experiment only.</p><h2>Recommendation and remaining limitations</h2><p><strong>Keep A as the most promising prototype, but adopt none yet.</strong> A removes the dominant topology artifact most economically. B and C have not produced convincing chunky sandstone, despite technically valid meshes. The visual goal is not yet met. The remaining problem is primary-form construction: the mass variants are displaced front skins whose inset seams read as plates, not naturally eroded volumes. The fixed top/bottom contour also preserves part of the original repeated silhouette. Solving those problems needs a better isolated mass prototype, not another whole-map filter or a parameter-only rollout.</p><p><strong>Stopped at the requested checkpoint.</strong> No A/B/C mode is enabled in the production executable. No changes to production canyon-generation source were made in this experiment; earlier uncommitted work remains as it was. No approval for a world-scale change is inferred. This experiment is uncommitted.</p><h2>Reproduce / temporary switches</h2><pre>cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build --target deathward_cliff_alternatives -j4
python3 tools/cliff_experiments/capture.py
python3 tools/cliff_experiments/report.py
node tools/cliff_experiments/export-sheets.cjs

# Live debug preview, same isolated wall:
DW_CLIFF_OPTION=a ./build/deathward_cliff_alternatives --smoke --theme canyon \\
  --style original --scene profile-works --frames 6000
# Options: original, a, b, c. Add DW_CLIFF_WIRE=1 for the mesh overlay.</pre><p class="small">The CMake diagnostic target generates an instrumented copy of CanyonScene.cpp in the build directory, with two explicit hooks. It compiles the normal game sources with that diagnostic renderer and the separate tools/cliff_experiments code. The normal deathward target still compiles the original renderer. No new assets, persistent settings, engine shader changes or gameplay switches are introduced.</p></main></html>'''
(out/'index.html').write_text(html)
print(json.dumps(stats,indent=2))
